    {
      "question": "e-13186",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "77e42859fabe5c6a3f1d38cf3e470cd45ae63c2170022dac3fbb510bff85ab26",
      "new_sha256": "80532ebd8b7135a53f92e8e378642acefe6b263eb6b90bf11b6ff5361f062c68",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-13186",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots, \\quad -5, \\quad -3, \\quad -1, \\quad 1, \\quad 3, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =-3-(-5) \\\\  & =-1-(-3) \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  $a_1=1,$ the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =1+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{2n-1 \\: : \\: n \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\big\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!** \n\nThe constructive definition of a set is typically not unique. \n\nSince the elements of $A$ are generated by a *two-way* infinite arithmetic sequence, we could have picked *any* term in our sequence as $a_1$ when determining $a_n.$ We selected $a_1 = 1$ because this led to a nice, simple expression in our constructive definition.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13186.json",
          "file_sha256": "4e28a5a983680d8835a838216b2c38bb985188b593a2bc0268a30289396271d9"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1407,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1408
    },
    {
      "question": "e-13184",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "1890ab084442aca7d0c65ca33273369732af32701bc5f1e79022d372e8ff6751",
      "new_sha256": "23996bb1ce85d5aaf3c806e2a400cd95329a662310cab3770973a14b28eef1b6",
      "category": "ma_capture",
