      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-13144",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-9$ and $5$ (including $-9$ and $5$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS = \\{ x \\in \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\mathbb Z} \\: : \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-9} \\leq x \\leq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5} \\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example, we can write $S$ equivalently as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{ x \\in \\mathbb Z \\: : \\: -10 \\lt x \\lt 6 \\big\\}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13144.json",
