      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-13185",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The given set contains the roots $z\\in\\mathbb C$ of some quadratic polynomial $f(z).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots $z_1=-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z-(-3\\text{i}))(z-(3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z+3\\text{i})(z-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}+9) \\\\  & =4{z}^{2}+36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\: : \\: 4z^2+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}z+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}36} = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=0$ and $q=36.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13185.json",
          "file_sha256": "e31073c8c1948cad40bb127a3a64a0f40b2aed3a713ab0c190e95d65180c2a2d"
        }
